  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Describe the set $S=\\{-4,-3,-2,-1,0,1,…\\}$ using a conditional definition.\n\n$$\nS=\\{x\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,x>{{field-2}}\\}\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "The set $S$ contains all integers greater than $-4,$ including $-4.$\n\nIn other words, $S$ contains all integers greater than $-5,$ *excluding* $-5.$ \n\nTherefore, the set can be written as\n\n$$\nS=\\{x\\in Z\\,:\\,x>-5\\}.\n$$\n\n**Note**: This definition is not unique. For example:\n\n- We can write $x\\ge -4.$ This gives\n\n$$\nS=\\{x\\in Z\\,:\\,x\\ge -4\\}.\n$$",
